   231	## 4. Theorem TAIL-SPLIT: what the closed indexed forms actually give
   232	
   233	### 4.1 The b3-degree of the tail is at most two, uniformly
   234	
   235	`wt(b3) = t+1` and `deg_wp T_{t,2t-1-r} = 2t+2+r <= 3t+1 < 3(t+1)`, so no
   236	monomial of a tail row can carry `b3^3`.  Writing the rows as polynomials in
   237	`b3` over `P_t`,
   238	
   239	```text
   240	T_{t,2t-1-r} = a_r b3^2 + b_r b3 + c_r,
   241	wt(a_r) = r,  wt(b_r) = t+1+r,  wt(c_r) = 2t+2+r,   all in P_t.        (4.1)
   242	```
   243	
   244	Since `wt(a_r) = r`, the form `a_r` can only involve `b4, q_{2,0}, .., q_{r,0}`;
   245	in particular `a_0` has weight 0, i.e. `a_0 in A_t`.  These are the charged
   246	fable5 statements (3.1)-(3.2), re-derived from the weights alone.  Verified on
   247	regenerated rows at `t=2,3,4,5`: the support of `a_r` is exactly
   248	`{b4, q_{2,0}, .., q_{r,0}}`, its weight is exactly `r`, and its term count is
   249	the number of partitions of `r` into parts `<= t-1` (`1,1,2,3,5` at `t=5`), so
   250	every allowed monomial occurs (`tail_audit_t{2,3,4,5}.out`).
   251	
   252	### 4.2 The unit
   253	
   254	The banked symbolic-`t` b3-axis extraction
   255	(`k16-terminal-proof-sol56-20260903.md` (6.1)-(6.2)) gives, as an identity in
   256	`Q(t)[d]/(3d^2-t-1)`,
   257	
   258	```text
   259	a_0 = -alpha_t,
   260	alpha_t = t(3t+1)(A_b d + B_b) / (12 q^2 (3t-1)^2 (3t+2)),
   261	A_b = 27t^3-30t^2+t-2,   B_b = 6t^3+13t^2-3t+2.                        (4.2)
   262	```
   263	
   264	I re-derived its norm from scratch in `alpha_norm_audit.py`:
   265	
   266	```text
   267	Res_y(H_t, A_b d + B_b) = 4q^2 (3B_b^2 - A_b^2(t+1))
   268	   = -4 (t-2) (2t+1)^2 (3t-1)^2 (3t+2) (27t^3+17t^2+t+2).              (4.3)
   269	```
   270	
   271	The factorisation is exact (difference from the charged (3.6) is identically
   272	zero).  Its only integer root is `t=2`: `(3t-1)^2` and `(3t+2)` have no integer
   273	root, and `27t^3+17t^2+t+2` has the single real root `-0.720814492060...`.
   274	Hence
   275	
   276	```text
   277	alpha_t is a UNIT of A_t for every integer t>=3 (and t=1), on BOTH factors at
   278	every split index; at t=2 it is a zero divisor.                        (4.4)
   279	```
   280	
   281	(4.2) was independently confirmed here at `t=2,3,4,5`: `a_0 + alpha_t = 0`
