   540	### 7.2 The exact criterion
   541	
   542	Let `N` be the `(t-1) x 2` matrix over `P_t` with rows `(C_r, B_r)`.  A point of
   543	`V(J_t^tail)` over `p in Spec P_t` is a `beta` with `N(p) (1, beta)^T = 0` and
   544	`T_{t,2t-1}(p,beta) = 0`.  Hence, for `t>=3`:
   545	
   546	```text
   547	V(J_t^tail) = {0}
   548	  <=>  (i)  V(B_1,..,B_{t-1},C_1,..,C_{t-1}) = {0} in Spec P_t,  and
   549	       (ii) for every p != 0 with rank N(p) = 1 and ker N(p) spanned by a vector
   550	            of nonzero first coordinate, W_r(p) != 0 for some r.
   551	```
   552	
   553	(If `rank N(p) = 0` at some `p != 0` then, `a_0` being a unit,
   554	`T_{t,2t-1}(p, .)` has a root and `V(J)` acquires a positive-dimensional
   555	component -- this is clause (i).)  Clause (ii) is the residual content, and its
   556	shape is the reason no Groebner-free proof has been reached: the locus
   557	`rank N <= 1` of a `(t-1) x 2` matrix in a `(t-1)`-dimensional space has expected
   558	codimension `t-2`, i.e. expected dimension `1`.  So the statement to be proved
   559	for all `t` is a non-vanishing along a *curve* of candidate directions -- one
   560	scalar per component -- and the scalars are values of `b_r, c_r`, which the
   561	charged analysis shows carry the whole `2t+1`-step spine and admit no closed form
   562	in `t` by this route (fable5 Sec. 3(c); sol56 Sec. 6.3, where even the next
   563	coordinate axis `u_2` reduces only to an unfactored norm).  At `t=3,4,5` all
   564	`binom(t-1,2)` minors `B_r C_{r'} - B_{r'} C_r` are nonzero with the predicted
   565	weights `3t+3+r+r'` (1, 3 and 6 minors respectively;
   566	`tail_audit_t{3,4,5}.out` Sec. F), so clause (i) is not violated at those
   567	indices.
   568	
   569	### 7.3 Where the deep sub-charts sit in this picture
   570	
   571	On `S = {b4 = q_{2,0} = .. = q_{t-2,0} = 0}` with the single residual
   572	`x = q_{t-1,0}` of weight `t-1`, a coefficient survives only if its weight is a
   573	multiple of `t-1`.  So `a_0` survives (weight 0, the constant `-alpha_t`),
   574	`a_r|_S = 0` for `1<=r<=t-2` while `a_{t-1}|_S` is a scalar times `x`; `b_r|_S`
   575	vanishes except at `r=t-3` (the only multiple `2(t-1)` of `t-1` in
   576	`[t+1,2t]`), giving `beta x^2`; and `c_r|_S` vanishes except at `r=t-5`, when
   577	`t>=5` (the only multiple `3(t-1)` of `t-1` in `[2t+2,3t+1]`), giving
   578	`gamma x^3`.  For `t>=6` the tail therefore collapses on `S` to
   579	`{a_0 b3^2, (const) x b3^2, beta x^2 b3, gamma x^3}`, and dimension `0` there is
   580	exactly `gamma != 0` -- which is the banked `Q-PLANE` / `UNIQUE-POWER` step
   581	`T_{t,t+4}|_S = A2 x^3` (fable5 Sec. 5.2).  So the banked chain steps
   582	`(C_{t-r})`, `r<=5`, `t>=3r+3` are the deepest strata of criterion RANK, and the
   583	same cap `r <= (t-3)/3` applies.  Nothing in TAIL-SPLIT lifts that cap.
