   286	### 5.1 Promotion lemma (PROVED-HERE)
   287	
   288	Let `R` be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field `K` and residue field
   289	`kappa`, and `J` an ideal of `R[x_1,...,x_n]` generated by polynomials that
   290	are homogeneous for positive integer weights.  If the affine cone
   291	`V(J kappa[x])` is `{0}` over `kappabar`, then `V(J K[x])` is `{0}` over
   292	`Kbar`.  Proof: `X=Proj(R[x]/J)` is a closed subscheme of a weighted
   293	projective space over `Spec R`, hence proper over `Spec R`; its image is
   294	closed.  The special fibre is `Proj(kappa[x]/J)`, empty exactly when the
   295	cone modulo the maximal ideal is `{0}`; so the image misses the closed point,
   296	and the only closed subset of `Spec R` missing the closed point is empty.
   297	Hence `X` is empty and the generic fibre `Proj(K[x]/J)` is empty, i.e. the
   298	cone over `K` is `{0}`.
   299	
   300	Application.  Fix `t`, a prime `p` not dividing `12q^2` with a root `r` of
   301	`H_t` modulo `p`, and the prime `P=(p, y-r)` of `Z[y]/(H_t)`.  The rows
   302	`T_(t,k)` computed in `A_t` have coefficients `a+by` with `a,b` rational;
   303	Singular's evaluation of these at `y=r` in `GF(p)` fails loudly on a
   304	denominator divisible by `p` (`divzero_test.sing`: `? div. by 0` and
   305	`? error occurred`), and no such marker occurs in any modular `.out/.err`
   306	file used here (scanned for `div. by 0`, `div by 0`, `error occurred`).  Thus the rows lie in `R[x]` for the localisation `R` at
   307	`P`, whose fraction field is `A_t` (a field for non-split `t`; for split `t`
   308	each rational fibre is treated with `R=Z_(p)`), and the modular `JPLUS
   309	dim=0` on one root is a characteristic-zero proof that
   310	`V(T_(t,1),...,T_(t,2t-1))={0}`, hence of (8.1) and of (T) at that `t`.  This
   311	is the *safe* direction: an inhomogeneous unit ideal modulo `p` proves
   312	nothing (FALLACY-v2), but emptiness of a proper family is an open condition
   313	on the base.  Negative control: at `t=2`, `y=1/5`, the cone has dimension one
   314	exactly (the b3-axis) and dimension one modulo `32003`; the lemma's
   315	contrapositive (nonempty generic fibre forces nonempty special fibre) is
   316	satisfied.
