+## 6. FALLACY-v2 Audit
+
+- Flag/place/series: the CI series `P_t`, the EN curve `Gamma`, the affine cone
+  `V(I_{t,+})`, and z-type chart points are kept separate.
+- Floor/attainment: `L_t` is used only as the length after dimension zero or a
+  regular-sequence hypothesis is known.  It is not used to prove dimension zero
+  or top-row nonvanishing.
+- Carrier/attainment: the EN degree counts weighted points where Target A must
+  be checked; it is not a witness that the top row avoids them.
+- `sat()` wrapping: no saturation is used.
+- Raw remainder degree: the only normal-form style statement used here is the
+  generic eliminant identity in indeterminates, reproduced by the frozen driver.
+- Variable/ring map: the `t=8` computations explicitly use
+  `GF(32003)[b3,b4,q(2),...,q(7)]` with weights `wp(9,1,2,...,7)` and the sealed
+  row file at root `11288`.
+- Prime label/derivative: `p` is always a finite-field characteristic; prime
+  marks from Laurent formulas are not used as derivatives here.
+- Modular promotion: only homogeneous cone `dim=0` statements are promoted
+  through the charged properness gate.  Rabinowitsch radical membership modulo
+  `p` is not promoted.
+- No interpolation: no all-t certificate is inferred from the fixed range
+  `t<=7`.
+
+## 7. Final Status
+
+Target A is reduced uniformly to a clean EN/incidence nonvanishing problem:
+
+```text
+Sigma_t = V(C_r + beta B_r),
+Q_t = a_0 beta^2+b_0 beta+c_0,
+prove Sigma_t cap V(Q_t) has no nonzero point.
