+# K16 NZD/Gamma Lane Report
+
+Date: 2026-09-04
+
+Lane: `k16-nzd-gamma-gpt55-20260903`
+
+Work directory: `box/k16nzd-20260903/`
+
+Requested output: `xmodel/k16-nzd-gamma-gpt55-20260903.md`
+
+## 0. Verdict
+
+```text
+TARGET A ((V0), top-tail nonzerodivisor): PARTIAL.
+
+Uniformly proved/charged and used here:
+  FITT, EN-CURVE, LENGTH-SPLIT, DOMINANT-LEADER, TAIL-SPLIT,
+  the explicit eliminant identity W_r in (T_top,G_r), and the exact
+  residual formulation on the Eagon-Northcott curve Gamma.
+
+Not proved:
+  the all-t nonvanishing of
+    Q_t(p,beta) = a_0 beta^2 + b_0 beta + c_0
+  at every rank-1 Gamma point.  LENGTH-SPLIT does not force it; it
+  describes the length after the relevant finiteness/nonvanishing
+  hypothesis is already in place.
+
+Fixed range:
+  tail/RANK clause (ii), equivalently the nonzerodivisor statement, is
+  charged exact at t=3,4 and promoted at t=5,6.  Clause (i), in the
+  cleaner B-HSOP form, is charged through t=8 and was not redone here.
+  The t=8 top-tail probe in this lane timed out at 1800 s.
+
+TARGET B ((8.1), tau_t in radical(I_{t,+})): PARTIAL.
+
+Proved fixed range:
+  exact at t=2 on both fibres; exact/promoted for t=3,4,5,6,7 through
+  the charged homogeneous cone/properness instrument.  This implies
+  theorem (T) at those t through the banked reduction chain.
+
+Not proved:
+  no uniform Rabinowitsch certificate was found, and none is contained
+  in the charged inputs.  The t=8 b4=0 half is proved, RESIDUAL-ZERO at
+  t=8 is proved, but the t=8 b4=1 z-chart timed out at 1800 s here.
+```
+
+No exit-price assertion is made in this report, so no `charge_basis` line is
+due under `FALLACY-v2`.
+
+## 1. Custody And Mechanical Hash Check
+
+The frozen inputs were verified before the skeleton was written.  The manifest
+was generated mechanically from
+`xmodel/k16-nzd-gamma-gpt55-20260903.run.v2`, pairing its
+`charged_input_<i>_basename=` and `charged_input_<i>_sha256=` lines with `awk`;
+no hash digit was retyped.  The command wrote
+`box/k16nzd-20260903/charged_inputs.from_receipt.sha256` and
+`sha256sum -c` returned `OK` for all 12 charged inputs:
+
+```text
+k16-rank-criterion-fable5-20260903.md             OK
+k16-hsop-length-allt-opus5-20260903.md           OK
+k16-dep-locus-fable5-20260903.md                 OK
+k16-terminal-proof-fable5-20260903.md            OK
+k16-properness-gate-opus5-20260903.md            OK
+FALLACY-v2.md                                     OK
+eliminant_certificate.py                          OK
+ci_series_identity.py                             OK
+pure_power_sdr.py                                 OK
+tail_ideal_t3.py                                  OK
+crosscheck_norms.py                               OK
+tail_audit.py                                     OK
+```
+
+All new driver/output artifacts are in `box/k16nzd-20260903/`.  The artifact
+manifest `box/k16nzd-20260903/artifacts.sha256` excludes itself, verifies with
+`sha256sum -c`, and has SHA-256
+`3f80d2ba6acccb791699b027436bf34aea61d647a04b257a256b384c2d3c1bd6`.
+
+Operational notes:
+
+- Every shell job in this lane was launched in the foreground under
+  `timeout 1800 stdbuf -oL`.
+- The only long jobs used two cores total: the `t=8` `b4=1` z-chart and the
+  `t=8` top-tail cone.  Both reached timeout and exited 124.
+- No ledger, `jc2-lean`, `ideation-*`, or in-progress lane report was read or
+  edited.
+
+## 2. Charged Setting
+
+The charged notation is used unchanged.  Let
+
+```text
+q = 2t+1,
+H_t = 12q^2 y^2 - 12q(t+1)y + (t+1)(3t+2),
+A_t = Q[y]/(H_t),
+S_t = A_t[b4,q_{2,0},...,q_{t-1,0},b3],
+P_t = A_t[b4,q_{2,0},...,q_{t-1,0}].
+```
+
+Weights are
+
+```text
+wt(b4)=1, wt(q_{j,0})=j, wt(b3)=t+1,
+deg T_{t,k}=4t+1-k for k>=1,
+I_{t,+}=<T_{t,1},...,T_{t,2t-1}>,
+J_t^tail=<T_{t,t},...,T_{t,2t-1}>.
+```
+
+For the tail index `r=0,...,t-1`,
+
+```text
+T_{t,2t-1-r} = a_r b3^2 + b_r b3 + c_r,
+wt(a_r,b_r,c_r) = (r,t+1+r,2t+2+r).
+```
+
+The charged TAIL-SPLIT statement gives, for every `t>=3`,
+
+```text
+a_0 = -alpha_t is a unit in A_t,
+G_r := a_0 T_{t,2t-1-r} - a_r T_{t,2t-1} = B_r b3 + C_r,
+B_r = a_0 b_r - a_r b_0,
+C_r = a_0 c_r - a_r c_0.
+```
+
+Thus `S_t/(T_{t,2t-1})` is a free `P_t`-module on `{1,b3}`.  This is a
+structural fact about the top row itself, not the requested Target A
+nonzerodivisor statement, which is about multiplication by the top row on
+`S_t/(G_1,...,G_{t-1})`.
+
+The charged reports establish the exact b3-axis control:
+
+```text
+T_{t,2t-1}|axis = alpha_t b3^2,
+T_{t,t-2}|axis = beta_t b3^3,
+T_{t,0}|axis = -c,
+all other rows vanish on the axis,
+alpha_t,beta_t units for all t>=3 and both vanish exactly at t=2.
+```
+
+The exact `t=2` controls remain essential:
+
+```text
+t=2, y=1/5:
+  a_0=a_1=0, the cone has the b3-axis, (V0) fails,
+  but T0hom is in the radical with power 1, so (8.1) holds.
+
+t=2, y=2/5:
+  a_0=-28/625 is a unit, tail and full cone are zero-dimensional,
+  (V0) and (8.1) both hold.
+```
+
+## 3. Target A: Gamma And The Nonzerodivisor
+
+### 3.1 Exact Reformulation
+
+Let `N` be the `(t-1) x 2` matrix over `P_t` with rows `(C_r,B_r)`.  The charged
+FITT theorem identifies the 0-th Fitting ideal of `M_t/(G)M_t`, with
+`M_t=S_t/(T_{t,2t-1})`, as
+
+```text
+F_t = I_2(N) + (W_1,...,W_{t-1}) + (X_rs)_{r<s},
+W_r = a_0 C_r^2 - b_0 B_r C_r + c_0 B_r^2.
+```
+
+The explicit eliminant certificate, reproduced here in
+`box/k16nzd-20260903/eliminant_certificate.out`, is the identity
+
+```text
+W_r = B_r^2 T_{t,2t-1}
+      - G_r (a_0 G_r - 2 a_0 C_r + b_0 B_r).
+```
+
+The frozen driver prints
+
+```text
+W - [B^2 Q_0 - G(a0 G - 2a0 C + b0 B)] = 0
+Res_b3(Q_0,G) = B^2 c0 - B C b0 + C^2 a0 = W.
+```
+
+At a rank-1 point `p` of `N`, with kernel spanned by `(1:beta)`, we have
+`C_r(p)=-beta B_r(p)`.  Therefore
+
+```text
+W_r(p) = B_r(p)^2 Q_t(p,beta),
+X_rs(p) = B_r(p)B_s(p) Q_t(p,beta),
+Q_t(p,beta) = a_0 beta^2 + b_0 beta + c_0
+             = T_{t,2t-1}(p,beta).
+```
+
+Consequently, after clause (i) excludes nonzero rank-0 points, Target A is
+exactly:
+
+```text
+Q_t(p,beta) != 0
+for every nonzero p in Gamma = V(I_2(N)) with rank N(p)=1.
+```
+
+Equivalently, `T_{t,2t-1}` is a nonzerodivisor on
+`S_t/(G_1,...,G_{t-1})`.
+
+### 3.2 EN-Curve Parametrisation
+
+The usable parametrisation is the incidence description, not a closed formula
+for all coordinates.  Define
+
+```text
+Sigma_t = V(C_r + beta B_r, r=1..t-1)
+          inside Spec P_t x A^1_beta.
+```
+
+On the open where not all `B_r` vanish, projection
+`Sigma_t -> Gamma=V(I_2(N))` is an isomorphism over the rank-1 locus and beta is
+the kernel coordinate.  Clause (i), or the stronger charged B-HSOP statement,
+removes nonzero points with all `B_r=C_r=0`; it also removes the kernel
+`(0:1)` obstruction.  Thus the card's "kernel is `(1:beta)` and `(C_r,B_r)`
+are proportional" is exactly this incidence scheme.
+
+What is missing is a closed lower-dimensional base with closed-form coordinates
+for the rank-1 points.  The charged rank report explains why: the `B_r,C_r`
+have full support, and the `b_r,c_r` coefficients are spine-complete
+`t`-indexed sequences.  The EN complex gives the Hilbert series and weighted
+degree of the curve once the expected height is known, but it does not
+parametrise the individual points at which `Q_t` must be evaluated.
+
+The charged EN-CURVE formula is
+
+```text
+Hilb(P_t/I_2(N);s)
+ = [ prod_{r=1}^{t-1}(1-s^{2t+2+r})
+     - s^{t+1} prod_{r=1}^{t-1}(1-s^{t+1+r}) ]
+   / [ (1-s^{t+1}) prod_{i=1}^{t-1}(1-s^i) ],
+
+d_Gamma(t)
+ = [ C(3t+1,t-1) - C(2t,t-1) ] / (t+1).
+```
+
+This is a uniform structural theorem.  It reduces Target A to finitely many
+scalar nonvanishings per `t`, but it does not compute those scalars in closed
+form.
+
+### 3.3 Leading Coefficient Of The Quadratic
+
+The top row restricted to the incidence curve is
+
+```text
+Q_t(p,beta)=a_0 beta^2+b_0 beta+c_0,
+a_0=-alpha_t.
+```
+
+The charged alpha norm is
+
+```text
+Res_y(H_t, A_b d + B_b)
+ = -4 (t-2)(2t+1)^2(3t-1)^2(3t+2)
+     (27t^3+17t^2+t+2),
+```
+
+so `a_0` is a unit for every integer `t>=3` and on both factors at split
+indices.  This proves the quadratic is genuinely degree two in beta.  It does
+not prove it is nonzero at every Gamma point; the missing claim is not leading
+degree, but disjointness:
+
+```text
+Sigma_t cap V(Q_t) = {0}.
+```
+
+No all-t resultant or intersection certificate for this disjointness was found
+in the charged inputs or in this lane.
+
+### 3.4 LENGTH-SPLIT Does Not Force Target A
+
+The charged length identity is
+
+```text
+L_t = 2 C(3t+1,t-1)
+    = 2 C(2t,t-1) + (2t+2) d_Gamma(t).
+```
+
+The small CI driver was rerun here:
+`box/k16nzd-20260903/ci_series_identity_t16.out` prints
+`ALL_IDENTITY_CHECKS_PASS = True` through `t=16`, including
+
+```text
+L_3=90, L_4=572, L_5=3640, L_6=23256, L_7=149226,
+L_8=961400, L_9=6216210, L_10=40320150.
+```
+
+The identity has the following precise meaning.  If the relevant complete
+intersection is zero-dimensional, then its length decomposes into the b3-axis
+contribution
+
+```text
+2 C(2t,t-1)
+```
+
+and the residual Gamma contribution
+
+```text
+(2t+2) d_Gamma(t).
+```
+
+The factor `2` is the order of the top row on the b3-axis:
+`T_{t,2t-1}|axis = alpha_t b3^2`.  The factor `2t+2` is the weighted degree of
+the top row cutting each non-axis rank-1 line where the scalar `Q_t(p,beta)` is
+nonzero.
+
+This does not prove nonvanishing.  If `Q_t(p,beta)=0` on a Gamma component, then
+the top row vanishes identically on the corresponding residual line of
+`V(G_1,...,G_{t-1})`; the tail quotient is not a finite complete intersection
+there, and the finite length `L_t` is not available as a contradiction.  Using
+`L_t` to force the scalar nonvanishing would reverse the charged implication
+`dim=0 -> length=L_t`.  The charged DEGREE-BLIND theorem gives the exact
+control: at `t=2` the two fibres have identical weights and predicted length
+data, while `y=1/5` has dimension 1 and `y=2/5` has dimension 0.
+
+Thus LENGTH-SPLIT is a map of the residual problem, not a proof of Target A.
+
+### 3.5 Fixed-Range Computation
+
+The charged RANK report gives:
+
+```text
+clause (i) / B-HSOP:
+  t=3,4,5 exact; t=6,7,8 promoted or charged as settled through t=8.
+
+clause (ii) / nonzerodivisor:
+  t=3,4 exact; t=5,6 promoted.
+
+t=2 controls:
+  y=1/5 failure; y=2/5 success.
+```
+
+This lane did not redo clause (i), as requested.  It did attempt a new fixed
+`t=8` Target A probe using the sealed terminal row file
+`box/k16terminal-fable5-20260903/t8_p32003_r11288_rows.txt`, whose SHA-256
+matches that terminal lane's `SHA256SUMS.final`:
+
+```text
+5c81d527622cf69ae8851ba02fed6dee989ae73b40fb12c05fbc0e63a3f15cb8
+```
+
+The local driver
+`box/k16nzd-20260903/probe_t8.py` emitted the top-tail ideal
+`<T_8,...,T_15>` over `GF(32003)` at root `11288`.  The log says:
+
+```text
+TOPT t=8 generators=8 timeout=1800
+```
+
+No `dim` line flushed.  The process exited 124 at the 1800-second timeout, and
+stdout contained only Singular's `halt 1`.  This is
+`INCONCLUSIVE_TIMEOUT`, not evidence against Target A.
+
+### 3.6 Target A Residual
+
+The exact residual left open is:
+
+```text
+For every t>=3, prove that
+  Q_t(p,beta)=a_0 beta^2+b_0 beta+c_0
+is nonzero at all nonzero points of
+  Sigma_t = V(C_r + beta B_r)
+after removing the origin/rank-0 locus by clause (i).
+```
+
+The EN degree counts the amount of work:
+
+```text
+d_Gamma(t) = [ C(3t+1,t-1) - C(2t,t-1) ] / (t+1).
+```
+
+At `t=3,4` the charged decomposition of `V(G)` explicitly checks the non-axis
+lines and finds the top row nonzero on each.  At `t=5,6` the Fitting/`I_2+(W)`
+cone computations supply the promoted characteristic-zero certificate.  For
+all `t`, no closed-form resultant or intersection computation of
+`Sigma_t cap V(Q_t)` was obtained.
+
+## 4. Target B: Direct Radical Membership
+
+### 4.1 Exact Statement
+
+Write
+
+```text
+T_{t,0} = -c + tau_t
+```
+
+in Fable's sign convention, with `tau_t=T^hom_{t,0}` homogeneous of weight
+`4t+1`.  The weaker JC2-sufficient statement is
+
+```text
+(8.1)  tau_t in sqrt(I_{t,+}),
+I_{t,+}=<T_{t,1},...,T_{t,2t-1}>.
+```
+
+Equivalently,
+
+```text
+V(I_{t,+}) cap D(tau_t) = empty.
+```
+
+The charged properness gate confirms that this is strictly weaker than
+`V(I_{t,+})={0}`.  The exact witness is the `t=2, y=1/5` fibre:
+
+```text
+JPLUS dim = 1,
+T0HOM_IN_RADICAL power = 1.
+```
+
+So a positive-dimensional cone is allowed, provided it is contained in
+`V(tau_t)`.
+
+### 4.2 What Properness Can And Cannot Promote
+
+For ideals generated by positive-weight homogeneous forms, the charged
+properness lemma promotes
+
+```text
+V(J mod p) = {0}  ->  V(J in characteristic zero) = {0}.
+```
+
+This is the sound direction used for `I_{t,+}` when `JPLUS dim=0` modulo a good
+prime.  It proves a stronger statement than (8.1).
+
+It does not promote Rabinowitsch radical membership.  The Rabinowitsch test is
+
+```text
+I_{t,+} + (1 - z tau_t) = (1)
+```
+
+in an affine ring with a new variable `z`.  That ideal is not a positive-weight
+homogeneous cone in the sense needed by the properness lemma.  The charged
+properness report gives the model failure:
+
+```text
+R=Z_(p), J=(x-py), tau=x:
+tau in sqrt(J mod p), but tau notin sqrt(J over Frac(R)).
+```
+
+Therefore a modular Rabinowitsch unit ideal is evidence only.  To prove Target B
+uniformly one needs an exact all-t certificate, for example
+
+```text
+tau_t^N in I_{t,+}
+```
+
+with `N` and all cofactors given by closed expressions in `t`, or another exact
+argument that every cone component lies in `V(tau_t)`.  No such certificate is
+in the charged inputs, and this lane did not find one.
+
+### 4.3 Relation To Z-Type Pairs
+
+The charged dependency-locus report identifies the geometric meaning of
+`tau_t=0`.  For every residual point `p`,
+
+```text
+J(Q_p,P_p) = c gamma + pi E_t(h),
+E_t(h) = sum_{k=0}^{2t-1} T_{t,k}(p) h^k.
+```
+
+On the cone `V(I_{t,+})`, this becomes a linear form controlled by `T_{t,0}`.
+The condition `tau_t(p)=0` is the z-type case
+
+```text
+J = c(gamma - pi) = -c z.
+```
+
+This explains why `t=2,y=1/5` is not a counterexample to theorem (T): the
+positive-dimensional b3-axis component is z-type and lies in `V(tau_2)`.
+
+It also explains the residual obstruction for Target B.  Proving (8.1) directly
+requires excluding cone points with `tau_t != 0`, not necessarily excluding all
+cone points.
+
+### 4.4 Fixed Range And The t=8 Boundary
+
+The charged terminal/properness reports prove:
+
+```text
+t=2:
+  both rational fibres exact; (8.1) holds on y=1/5 and y=2/5.
