+
+## 0. Verdict
+
+```text
+TARGET A ((V0), top-tail nonzerodivisor): PARTIAL.
+
+Uniformly proved/charged and used here:
+  FITT, EN-CURVE, LENGTH-SPLIT, DOMINANT-LEADER, TAIL-SPLIT,
+  the explicit eliminant identity W_r in (T_top,G_r), and the exact
+  residual formulation on the Eagon-Northcott curve Gamma.
+
+Not proved:
+  the all-t nonvanishing of
+    Q_t(p,beta) = a_0 beta^2 + b_0 beta + c_0
+  at every rank-1 Gamma point.  LENGTH-SPLIT does not force it; it
+  describes the length after the relevant finiteness/nonvanishing
+  hypothesis is already in place.
+
+Fixed range:
+  tail/RANK clause (ii), equivalently the nonzerodivisor statement, is
+  charged exact at t=3,4 and promoted at t=5,6.  Clause (i), in the
+  cleaner B-HSOP form, is charged through t=8 and was not redone here.
+  The t=8 top-tail probe in this lane timed out at 1800 s.
+
+TARGET B ((8.1), tau_t in radical(I_{t,+})): PARTIAL.
+
+Proved fixed range:
+  exact at t=2 on both fibres; exact/promoted for t=3,4,5,6,7 through
+  the charged homogeneous cone/properness instrument.  This implies
+  theorem (T) at those t through the banked reduction chain.
+
+Not proved:
+  no uniform Rabinowitsch certificate was found, and none is contained
+  in the charged inputs.  The t=8 b4=0 half is proved, RESIDUAL-ZERO at
+  t=8 is proved, but the t=8 b4=1 z-chart timed out at 1800 s here.
+```
+
+No exit-price assertion is made in this report, so no `charge_basis` line is
+due under `FALLACY-v2`.
+
+## 1. Custody And Mechanical Hash Check
+
