+## 4. Target B: Direct Radical Membership
+
+### 4.1 Exact Statement
+
+Write
+
+```text
+T_{t,0} = -c + tau_t
+```
+
+in Fable's sign convention, with `tau_t=T^hom_{t,0}` homogeneous of weight
+`4t+1`.  The weaker JC2-sufficient statement is
+
+```text
+(8.1)  tau_t in sqrt(I_{t,+}),
+I_{t,+}=<T_{t,1},...,T_{t,2t-1}>.
+```
+
+Equivalently,
+
+```text
+V(I_{t,+}) cap D(tau_t) = empty.
+```
+
+The charged properness gate confirms that this is strictly weaker than
+`V(I_{t,+})={0}`.  The exact witness is the `t=2, y=1/5` fibre:
+
+```text
+JPLUS dim = 1,
+T0HOM_IN_RADICAL power = 1.
+```
+
+So a positive-dimensional cone is allowed, provided it is contained in
+`V(tau_t)`.
+
+### 4.2 What Properness Can And Cannot Promote
+
+For ideals generated by positive-weight homogeneous forms, the charged
+properness lemma promotes
+
+```text
+V(J mod p) = {0}  ->  V(J in characteristic zero) = {0}.
+```
+
+This is the sound direction used for `I_{t,+}` when `JPLUS dim=0` modulo a good
+prime.  It proves a stronger statement than (8.1).
+
+It does not promote Rabinowitsch radical membership.  The Rabinowitsch test is
+
+```text
+I_{t,+} + (1 - z tau_t) = (1)
+```
+
+in an affine ring with a new variable `z`.  That ideal is not a positive-weight
+homogeneous cone in the sense needed by the properness lemma.  The charged
+properness report gives the model failure:
+
+```text
+R=Z_(p), J=(x-py), tau=x:
+tau in sqrt(J mod p), but tau notin sqrt(J over Frac(R)).
+```
+
+Therefore a modular Rabinowitsch unit ideal is evidence only.  To prove Target B
+uniformly one needs an exact all-t certificate, for example
+
+```text
+tau_t^N in I_{t,+}
+```
+
+with `N` and all cofactors given by closed expressions in `t`, or another exact
+argument that every cone component lies in `V(tau_t)`.  No such certificate is
+in the charged inputs, and this lane did not find one.
+
+### 4.3 Relation To Z-Type Pairs
+
+The charged dependency-locus report identifies the geometric meaning of
+`tau_t=0`.  For every residual point `p`,
+
+```text
+J(Q_p,P_p) = c gamma + pi E_t(h),
+E_t(h) = sum_{k=0}^{2t-1} T_{t,k}(p) h^k.
+```
+
+On the cone `V(I_{t,+})`, this becomes a linear form controlled by `T_{t,0}`.
+The condition `tau_t(p)=0` is the z-type case
+
+```text
+J = c(gamma - pi) = -c z.
+```
+
